.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ECCE-QM, B3LYP-D3(BJ)/def2-SVP, transition-state optimisation and frequencies, orbitals localised. This calculation shows the keto-enol transition state with one water molecule as a proton relay, with one imaginary mode at -1763.05 cm-1, a six-membered ring in which one proton moves from carbon to water (C-H 1.471 Å, H-O 1.209 Å) while another moves from water to the carbonyl oxygen (O-H 1.178 Å, H-O 1.265 Å), and an electronic energy of -269.187898 Eh, 103.4 kJ/mol above acetone plus water.
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ECCE-QM
